Ah, there's a different price for angering a peaceful than for
popcorning a peaceful all the way to death in one blow:

		adjalign(-1);		/* attacking peaceful monsters is bad */

I think you were at zero and that one point was enough to go negative. 
The partially absolved message is ambiguous because it looks like it can
be given even if your numerical alignment goes from negative to zero.

I think you were safe to pray before you attacked the pony.  You had
seen a clover.  Then angering it pushed your alignment negative, saccing
it pushed your alignment to zero.

I bet the next sac after turn 9911 will show a clover.


